###########################################################################
# NativeGlobalIndexPort1624 - 전제와 판별자
#
# 이 스위트의 전 케이스가 재는 것은 **디스크 파티션드 테이블 위의 네이티브
# 글로벌 인덱스**다. 원본(qp4/Project3/PROJ-1624-GlobalIndex)이 같은 문장으로
# 재던 것은 숨김 테이블 $GIT_ 였다. 갈림길은 프로퍼티 하나다:
#
#   DISK_GLOBAL_INDEX_ENABLE = 1  -> 네이티브 (이 스위트)
#   DISK_GLOBAL_INDEX_ENABLE = 0  -> $GIT_    (원본 스위트)
#
# ★ 그래서 케이스마다 자기 전제를 세운다(F07 규약).
#   파일 기본값은 2026-08-06 부터 1 이지만, 기본값에 기대면 그 값이 움직이는
#   날 이 스위트는 "네이티브를 잰다"고 적어 놓고 $GIT_ 를 재게 된다 --
#   원본 PROJ-1624 와 NATC ddl/diskPartitionedTable.tc 가 실제로 그렇게
#   어긋났었다(disk-natc.md 6).
#
# ★ 이 프로퍼티는 비영속이다. ALTER SYSTEM 값은 재기동하면 파일 값으로
#   돌아간다. 한 인스턴스 위에서 스위트가 이어 도는 동안은 FINALIZE 의
#   복원이 유일한 방벽이다.
###########################################################################

#
# 전제를 세우고, 세운 값을 전사에 남긴다.
# 전사가 자기 전제를 적게 하는 것이 목적이므로 v$property 조회를 뺄 수 없다.
#
DEF PIN_DISK_NATIVE()
{
  set linesize 200;
  alter system set DISK_GLOBAL_INDEX_ENABLE = 1;
  select cast(value1 as varchar(10)) disk_global_index_enable from v$property
  where name = 'DISK_GLOBAL_INDEX_ENABLE';
}
###########################################################################
# TestCase Description = ported from qp4/Project3/PROJ-1624-GlobalIndex/tool/aexport/initialize.tc
#
# Body below is byte-identical to the original. What this port adds is the
# premise: PIN_DISK_NATIVE() pins DISK_GLOBAL_INDEX_ENABLE = 1 and writes
# the value into the transcript, so the case states what it measures
# instead of inheriting it (F07 -- see include/globalIndexEnv.i).
#
# Project ID           = Native Global Index (disk) - PROJ-1624 port
###########################################################################

###########################################################################
# Check Constraint Test
###########################################################################

##########################################################################
# PORT EDIT: stdFunc.i goes with the three calls below
#
# Original line 5 was "INCLUDE stdFunc.i;". The only thing this case used it
# for is stdServerKill/stdClean/stdServerStart, and the next PORT EDIT
# removes those three -- see it for the reason. Nothing else in this file
# calls a std* DEF, so the include goes too rather than sitting here as a
# fragment that binds $gStdIsqlSys to this workflow's isolated instance.
##########################################################################
##########################################################################
# PORT EDIT END
##########################################################################

DEF MAIN()
{
CALL PIN_DISK_NATIVE();

##################################
# SECTOR; CLEAN
##################################

NODISPLAY ON;
##########################################################################
# PORT EDIT: do not recreate the database this workflow runs on
#
# Original lines 14-16 were:
#
#   CALL stdServerKill();
#   CALL stdClean();
#   CALL stdServerStart();
#
# stdClean() is destroydb + createdb: it drops "mydb" and creates it again
# with the character set KO16KSC5601. In the official harness that is how a
# case gets a known database. Here it is not available:
#
#   * this runner points ALTIBASE_HOME at the workflow's isolated instance
#     (scripts/global-index/testdb.sh, port 20399), and that instance is
#     UTF8. Every golden file, every baseline tsv and every other .lst in
#     this port was recorded on a UTF8 database. Recreating it as
#     KO16KSC5601 from inside one case would move all of them.
#   * the freshness stdClean() exists to provide is already provided, and
#     provided earlier: this suite carries NEEDS_FRESH_INSTANCE, so
#     natc-check.sh destroys and rebuilds the instance before the suite
#     starts (v4-natc-port.md 6.4).
#   * stdServerKill()/stdServerStart() go with it: they are how stdClean()
#     is bracketed, and on their own they would only bounce an instance
#     that natc-check.sh just started.
#
# What stays is the part these four cases exist for -- installing the
# DBMS_METADATA package, without which aexport stops at
# [ERR-91144 : DBMS_METADATA package does not exist.] and the three cases
# after this one measure nothing (v2-regression-net.md 4 recorded exactly
# that error for these four and left it there).
##########################################################################
##########################################################################
# PORT EDIT END
##########################################################################
EXEC P1 "is -f ${ALTIBASE_HOME}/packages/dbms_metadata.sql";
P_WAIT P1;
EXEC P1 "is -f ${ALTIBASE_HOME}/packages/dbms_metadata.plb";
P_WAIT P1;
NODISPLAY OFF;

}
